{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 12, :comments ["<b>I declared.</b> In Egypt, to save you." "<b>And I saved, and I caused you to hear.</b> My voice at Mount Sinai." "<b>And there was no stranger among you.</b> For Israel alone were there." "<b>And you are My witnesses.</b> And the meaning: you heard thus from the mouths of your fathers." "<b>And I am El.</b> Always, like the sense of 'I am YHWH, I have not changed' (Malachi 3:6)."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 43, :notes {4 "The manuscript reads ואני; the correction note צ״ל אני indicates the text should read simply אני."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:57:44.452224249Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}